{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJucysMurphyElements","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJucysMurphyElements","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneJucysMurphyTwist"],"declarations":24,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_jmRaw_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_jmRaw_one","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyElements.lean#L161-L170","doc":"`σⱼ` commutes with `L₂ = σ₀²` whenever `j ≥ 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.contentSum_three_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.contentSum_three_eq","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyElements.lean#L155-L157","doc":"`c([3]) = 3`: the exponent above is the one-row content sum, tying this file's normalization to\n`theta_single_row_sq`'s exponent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jm_prod_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jm_prod_three","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyElements.lean#L145-L153","doc":"**`∏Lᵢ = q^{-3}·Δ²` at `n = 3`** in the `q`-normalized convention, and `3 = c([3])`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jm_eq_smul_jmRaw_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jm_eq_smul_jmRaw_two","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyElements.lean#L138-L143","doc":"The two conventions differ by `q^{−i(i−1)/2}`.  Stated at the cases proved above; the exponent\n`i(i−1)/2` is `c([i])`, the same triangular number `two_mul_contentSum_single_row` feeds to the\ntwist — so the `q⁻¹` in the arc's convention is not free bookkeeping. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_prod_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_prod_three","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyElements.lean#L121-L134","doc":"**`∏Lᵢ = Δ²` at `n = 3`** — the first genuine case.\n\n`L₁L₂L₃ = σ₀σ₀ · σ₁σ₀σ₀σ₁`, and **one** application of the braid relation to the middle three\nletters (`σ₀σ₁σ₀ = σ₁σ₀σ₁`) turns it into `σ₀σ₁σ₀σ₁σ₀σ₁ = (σ₀σ₁)³`.  Only the braid relation is\nused — the Hecke relation is not needed for the twist identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_prod_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_prod_two","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyElements.lean#L115-L119","doc":"**`∏Lᵢ = Δ²` at `n = 2`** — immediate from the recursion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.fullTwist3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.fullTwist3","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyElements.lean#L112-L113","doc":"The full twist of `B₃`: `Δ² = (σ₀σ₁)³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.fullTwist2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.fullTwist2","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyElements.lean#L109-L110","doc":"The full twist of `B₂`: `Δ² = σ₀²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_closed_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_closed_two","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyElements.lean#L102-L105","doc":"**`L₂` in closed form**, by the Hecke relation: `L₂ = (q − q⁻¹)σ₀ + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jm_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jm_succ","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyElements.lean#L99-L100","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jm_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jm_zero","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyElements.lean#L97-L97","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_succ","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyElements.lean#L94-L95","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_zero","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyElements.lean#L92-L92","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jm","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyElements.lean#L87-L90","doc":"**`q`-normalized JM elements**: `L_{i+1} = q⁻¹ σᵢ Lᵢ σᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyElements.lean#L81-L85","doc":"**Unnormalized JM elements**: `L₁ = 1`, `L_{i+1} = σᵢ Lᵢ σᵢ`.  This convention is the one for\nwhich `∏Lᵢ = Δ²` holds on the nose. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGenerators.far","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGenerators.far","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyElements.lean#L75-L75","doc":"**Far commutation**, `|i − j| ≥ 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGenerators.braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGenerators.braid","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyElements.lean#L73-L73","doc":"**Braid relation**, adjacent generators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGenerators.hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGenerators.hecke","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyElements.lean#L71-L71","doc":"**The Hecke relation** `σᵢ² = (q − q⁻¹)σᵢ + 1` (§7a). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGenerators.σinv_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGenerators.σinv_mul","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyElements.lean#L69-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGenerators.mul_σinv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGenerators.mul_σinv","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyElements.lean#L68-L68","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGenerators.σinv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGenerators.σinv","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyElements.lean#L67-L67","doc":"Their inverses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGenerators.σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGenerators.σ","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyElements.lean#L65-L65","doc":"The braid generators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGenerators.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGenerators.mk","kind":"ctor","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyElements.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGenerators","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGenerators","kind":"class","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyElements.lean#L61-L75","doc":"**The type-A Hecke presentation.**  Generators indexed by `ℕ` (the stable algebra `H_∞(q)`),\ninvertible, satisfying the braid relations and the corpus's Hecke relation (§7a). ","signatureChunk":0}]}